{"availability":"available","full":"snugprotocol/snug","name":"snug","description":"Portable, user-owned AI apps — one file, persistent state, your choice of host and intelligence.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"TypeScript","stars":2,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-31T05:08:40Z","updated":"2026-10-15T01:29:09Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://snugprotocol.org","topics":["agents","ai","llm","local-first","mcp","micro-apps","protocol","typescript"],"demo":"https://playground.snugprotocol.org/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T00:52:13.019Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T00:52:13.019Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T00:52:13.019Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T02:10:53.472Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-17T00:52:13.019Z","stars":2,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An open protocol for portable, agent-backed personal software.","Describe a small app in chat and the agent writes it. It runs in a hard sandbox and thinks through the host's agent at runtime,","while the app and its accumulated state — code, data, versions, chats — live in one portable .snug file the user keeps."],"features":["The app's brain is the host agent. A Snug chess game doesn't embed a chess engine — it sends the board to the host LLM through a standard postMessage envelope and animates the reply. The app is a body; the agent is the…","You own your apps and your data. Everything — every app's code, ≥5 versions, its isolated database, your chats, your settings — lives in one portable .snug file (real SQLite, openable with ordinary tools, optionally…","It's embeddable. Any product can drop in the runner + SDK and let their users build micro apps powered by their existing AI assistant. Snug is a protocol + reference implementation — the hosted Playground is the demo,…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/snugprotocol/snug/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9272f98adc84df3b281a4d1edd09d1055